※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4404

※ The startup function takes what the program was started with, or nothing.  A
※ parameter of any other type is refused: there is nothing the entry point could
※ put in it, the descriptors being the only thing it has to hand over.
※
※ Nothing about the *shape* of the type is what decides it -- a record a program
※ defines for itself and calls `Init` is a record it defined for itself.  What
※ the compiler passes the descriptors to is the one type it knows, the one the
※ `std` module found beside the compiler wrote down.

type Init = io : u32

@[startup]
fn main(init: Init) → u6:
    if init.io = 0u32: 0u6 else: 1u6
